You are tailoring a resume for a specific job. You will perform JD analysis, project selection, and STAR bullet writing in a single structured response.

Return ONLY a JSON object with this exact schema:
{
  "jd_analysis": {
    "must_have_keywords": [string, ...],
    "nice_to_have_keywords": [string, ...],
    "semantic_themes": [string, ...],
    "seniority": string | null,
    "primary_responsibilities": [string, ...]
  },
  "selected_project_ids": [string, ...],     // 2-4 ids
  "selection_rationale": string,
  "headline": string,
  "summary": string,
  "skills": [string, ...],
  "experience": [
    {
      "company": string, "title": string, "start": string, "end": string | null,
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": string,
          "source": "experience",
          "source_ref": "experience:<company>:<start>",
          "star": {"s": "...", "t": "...", "a": "...", "r": "..."},
          "keywords_hit": [string, ...],
          "has_estimate": boolean
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "project_bullets": [
    {
      "text": string,
      "source": "project",
      "source_ref": "project:<project_id>",
      "star": {"s": "...", "t": "...", "a": "...", "r": "..."},
      "keywords_hit": [string, ...],
      "has_estimate": boolean
    }
  ],
  "cover_paragraph": string
}

HARD RULES:
- NEVER change company names, titles, or dates from the master resume.
- Each `bullets` entry's source_ref must trace to an experience the user actually has.
- Each `project_bullets` source_ref must reference one of the SELECTED project ids.
- At least 3 bullets per experience entry; 2–3 project_bullets per selected project id.
- If you ESTIMATE a metric, set has_estimate=true and put "[ESTIMATE]" inside the R clause text.
- STAR format: every bullet implies Situation, Task, Action, Result. Past-tense action verbs.
- >=90% of must_have_keywords must appear across the resume's skills+bullets.
- Output JSON only. No prose, no code fences.

JOB TITLE: {{ job.title }}
COMPANY: {{ job.company }}
JOB DESCRIPTION:
{{ job.description_text }}

MASTER RESUME:
Name: {{ master.name }}
Headline: {{ master.headline }}
Summary: {{ master.summary }}
Skills (verified): {{ master.skills | join(", ") }}
Experience:
{% for e in master.experience %}
- {{ e.company }} | {{ e.title }} | {{ e.start }} - {{ e.end or "Present" }}
  base bullets:
  {% for b in e.base_bullets %}    * {{ b }}
  {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

CANDIDATE PROJECTS (pick 2-4 most relevant, write project_bullets for them):
{% for p in candidates %}
- id: {{ p.id }}
  title: {{ p.title }}
  summary: {{ p.summary }}
  tech: {{ p.tech_stack | join(", ") }}
  metrics: {{ p.impact_metrics | join("; ") if p.impact_metrics else "(none)" }}
{% endfor %}
